To ensure that the polynomial has exactly one real root when $k = 2\sqrt[3]{32},$ we must consider which complex roots are real. Since $x_1$ and $x_2$ are complex conjugates, and their real parts are equal, we can conclude that the real root of the polynomial will be the number with the largest magnitude. We have:
