         &= 288\text{ m}^3
\end{align*}

Now, to find the volume of water when the pool is half full, we need to find half of the full volume:
\begin{align*}
V_\text{half} &= \frac{1}{2}V_\text{full}\\
         &= \frac{1}{2} × 288\text{ m}^3\\
         &= 144\text{ m}^3
\end{align*}

