It can be done in the following steps:

1. Simplify the expression under the square root:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{\dfrac{(\frac{4}{\sqrt{24}})+\frac{\sqrt{3456}}{9}+\sqrt6}{\sqrt6}} &= \sqrt{\dfrac{\frac{4}{\sqrt{6^3}}+\frac{\sqrt{3456}}{9}+\sqrt6}{\sqrt6}} \\
&= \sqrt{\dfrac{\frac{4}{6^{3/2}}+\frac{\sqrt{3456}}{6}+\sqrt6}{\sqrt6}} \\
&= \sqrt{\dfrac{\frac{4}{6}+\frac{\sqrt{3456}}{6}+\sqrt6}{\sqrt6}} \\
&= \sqrt{\dfrac{\frac{1}{3}+ \sqrt{\frac{3456}{6}}+\sqrt6}{\sqrt6}} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{1}{3} + \sqrt{\frac{576}{3}} + \sqrt{6 \cdot 6}} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{1}{3}+ 4 + \sqrt{36}} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{1}{3}+ 4 + 6} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{1}{3}+10}
\end{align*}

Now, we can factor 49 out of the numerator:
\begin{align*}
&= \sqrt{\frac{49 (\frac{1}{49} + 10)}{3}} \\
&= 7 \sqrt{\frac{1+\frac{10}{49}}{\frac{3}{49}}}  \\
&= 7 \sqrt{1+\frac{10}{49}} \sqrt{\frac{49}{3}}
\end{align*}

Here's the final answer:

\boxed{7 \sqrt{1+\frac{10}{49}} \sqrt{\frac{49}{3}} }

(If units are required, they would be in the form of a square root, but I don't believe this is necessary for this problem.)

