Now, with these angles in radians, it is possible to compute the arcsine (inverse sine) of each.$ \sin^{-1} (x)$ is also equivalent to $\arcsin (x)$ . To compute the arcsine we can use a reverse trig function formula, which looks uglier, but is generally recognized for backwards compatibility. The formula is: $\arcsin (x) = \sin^{-1} (x) = \sin^{-1} \left(\frac{2}{\sqrt{(1 + x^2) + \sqrt{4-x^2}}} \right)$

